; bfsodium KECCAK THETA : the theta step of Keccak_f{1600}  FIPS 202 section 3
;
; HAND WRITTEN; The first of the five steps of a Keccak round and the only one
; that mixes the columns; Every lane of the state takes the exclusive or of two
; whole columns  one to its left and one to its right turned by a single bit;
;
; INTERFACE entry=200 exit=0 footprint=0:361
; IO  in:  A{200}  twenty five 64 bit lanes  each little endian
;     out: A{200}  the same  with theta applied
;
; TAPE MAP  (home @0)
;   @0x000:0x0c7  A{200}   the state; lane k is at cell 8k  and lane k is the
;                          lane FIPS 202 calls A{x  y} where k is 5y plus x
;   @0x0c8:0x0cf  T{8}     the LOWER holding lane; a lane of the state is copied
;                          through it and handed straight back
;   @0x0d0:0x0f5  the exclusive or frame; xor64 footprint 0:37 pasted at @0x0d0
;                          so its x is @0x0d0  its y is @0x0d8 and its r @0x0e0
;   @0x0f6:0x11d  D{40}    five lanes; D{x} is what column x contributes
;   @0x11e:0x125  T1{8}    the UPPER holding lane  for C and for D
;   @0x126:0x14d  C{40}    five lanes; C{x} is the exclusive or of column x
;   @0x14e:0x169  the rotation frame; rotl64 footprint 0:27 pasted at @0x14e
;                          so its w is @0x14e and its n is @0x156
;
; THE STEP  in FIPS 202's own letters:
;
;   C{x} = A{x 0} xor A{x 1} xor A{x 2} xor A{x 3} xor A{x 4}
;   D{x} = C{x minus 1} xor rotl(C{x plus 1}  1)
;   A{x y} = A{x y} xor D{x}
;
; with both of the index arithmetics taken modulo five; A column is the five
; lanes 5y plus x for y nought to four  so a column is a STRIDE of five lanes
; or forty cells  and that stride is the only reason this step needs a frame at
; all: xor64 wants its two operands eight cells apart and no two lanes of a
; column ever are;
;
; WHY THE OPERANDS ARE CARRIED TO A FRAME rather than the frame pasted at the
; operands  which is what poly1305/mulmod136 was relaid to do: idiom/xor64
; CONSUMES both of its operands and writes its answer to a third place eight
; cells further on; So a paste over two lanes would destroy both and land its
; answer on a third lane; A lane that is still needed is copied  through a
; holding lane  and a lane that is finished is moved;
;
; THAT CARRYING IS THE COST OF THIS FILE  and it has now been MEASURED: on a
; random state theta ran sixty one million instructions  of which the fifty
; xor64s and the five rotl64s account for fourteen and a half million; The
; other SEVENTY SIX PER CENT was lanes travelling  and this map is what came of
; that measurement;
;
; THE MAP IS THE OPTIMISATION  because the arithmetic never changed; A move of
; one byte over d cells costs two instructions per cell per unit of the byte
; being moved  so a lane's journey costs twice its distance eight times over
; and NOTHING ELSE IN THIS FILE IS WORTH A THOUGHT UNTIL THE DISTANCES ARE
; SHORT; The state occupies cells nought to 199 and cannot move  so every frame
; is packed as close above it as it will go: the exclusive or frame sits at
; @0x0d0 where it used to sit at @0x120  and C and D  which are five lanes each
; and are read far less often than the state  were pushed above it instead;
;
; AND THERE ARE TWO HOLDING LANES rather than one  which is the part that is
; not obvious; A copy from s to e keeping s must visit e AND the holding lane
; and come back  so it costs twice the SPAN of those three cells; A lane coming
; UP out of the state wants its holding lane BELOW the frame  or the span
; reaches past the frame for nothing; C and D coming DOWN to the frame want one
; ABOVE it  for the same reason mirrored; One holding lane cannot be both  and
; a second costs eight cells;
;
; THE SUM OF EVERY DISTANCE IN THIS FILE  counted as instructions per unit of
; byte value  came to 47600 on the old map and comes to 32700 on this one;
; Measured end to end on the same random state that is 60962481 instructions
; before and 46787857 after  very nearly a quarter off a step that is entered
; twenty four times in every permutation;
;
; A COPY THROUGH A HOLDING LANE IS TWO RUNS  the first taking the lane to its
; destination and to the holding lane at once  the second bringing it back; A
; lane is eight cells and every byte of it travels the same distance  so each
; run is one repeated token  the way sha512/hashcore writes its long runs;
; Every distance below was worked out from the map above and written down;

; read the state little endian  leaving the pointer past it
  ,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>
